# Netlify headers (see docs.netlify.com/routing/headers).
# Security headers on everything; clip files are content-hashed (FNV-1a of
# the spoken string) so they can NEVER go stale -> immutable, 1 year.
# manifest.json files and pages deliberately keep Netlify's default
# max-age=0,must-revalidate. Wildcards are SEGMENT-scoped, and duplicate
# header names across matching rules get concatenated (RFC 7230) -- keep
# Cache-Control out of the /* block.

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()

/audio/*.mp3
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

